# Windows release version

A Windows installer uses the first version in `CHANGELOG.md`. Bump that version, and the same version in `meson.build`, before building the installer. Leave the previous number as its own section.

`scripts/ci/windows-package-nsis.sh` refuses to package when `meson.build` or the compiled `argus-agent.exe` is a different version. It also refuses when `dist-windows/ArgusAgent-{version}-Setup.exe` already exists. Reconfigure and rebuild after the bump. The agent window shows the compiled version.

The window title already appends `Argus.VERSION`. Do not ship a Windows build on a version that was already installed. Delete the old installer only when intentionally replacing that same version — normally bump instead.

## Output directory on `snappr-win`

The ONLY Windows installer directory on `snappr-win` is `C:\msys64\tmp\argusrm\dist-windows` (`/tmp/argusrm/dist-windows` in MSYS2). Build/package there and never put installers in `C:\Users\Alan\argus-pkg\dist-windows` or any other directory on `snappr-win`.
